course: dictionary
lesson: 12317
title: Checking a claim with corroboration
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Corroboration is extra evidence that shows a statement is true. When someone says something important, a careful thinker asks: can I find more proof? Each new piece of evidence that agrees with the claim is corroboration.
explain: «Ava said she saw an owl in the park.» Then her friend Ben saw it too and took a photo. Ben's photo is corroboration, because it makes Ava's claim much more believable.
explain: Corroboration is uncountable, so say «some corroboration», not «a corroboration». Look out for the phrases «without corroboration» (with no proof to back it up) and «in corroboration of» (to support something).
fact: Corroboration means extra evidence that shows something is true.
fact: «Corroboration» is uncountable: say «some corroboration», not «a corroboration».
fact: A claim without corroboration is not proven yet, so be careful before you believe it.
fact: «Independent corroboration» means proof from a separate source that does not depend on the first one.
fact: Journalists, detectives and scientists all look for corroboration before they trust a claim.
exercise: «Ava said she saw an owl in the park. Ben saw it too and took a photo.» Ben's photo is what kind of evidence? | A rumour | A question | A hobby | *Corroboration
exercise: What does «without corroboration» mean? | With a lot of extra proof | Very quickly | Loudly and clearly | *With no proof to back it up
exercise: Which sentence uses corroboration correctly? | The story needed a corroboration of the facts. | The story needed corroborations before we believed it. | *The story needed some corroboration before we believed it.
test:
test: What is the best meaning of corroboration? | *Extra evidence that shows a statement is true | A loud argument | A kind of map | A type of fast car
test: Ruby says her grandad's old map shows the right route. Which would be corroboration? | Nobody has looked at the map | A map that is blank | Ruby saying it again, louder | *A second map and an old diary that show the same route
exam: Which phrase means that a separate source, not the first one, backs up a claim? | *Independent corroboration | Without corroboration | In corroboration of
